-- Rifts World Book 17: Warlords of Russia - its bestiary and its notable NPCs.
-- 5 creatures (migration 074) and 8 notable NPCs (migration 072),
-- with their attacks in stat_attacks (migration 073).
--
-- One-off data script, run once per environment. NOT a migration.
--
--   node scripts/d1-apply.mjs --local apps/character-creator/db/add-warlords-of-russia-bestiary.sql
--
-- Written by scripts/bestiary-sql.mjs from 2 worker file(s). Every
-- creature row passes creatureFormulaGaps, every value is printable ASCII,
-- and an 8-word shingle check of the prose fields against the book's cached text finds no copied run.
-- Rifts World Book 17: Warlords of Russia, batches 7 and 8: the five Mega-Steeds
-- (printed 164-170) as creatures and eight notable NPCs - the seven Warlords
-- (printed 37-56) and General Katya Nikoforov of the Sovietski (printed 207).
--
-- Every row was checked against the page by book-reconcile before the apply:
-- 13 rows, no figure disagreed.
--
-- READ OFF A RENDER: the True Megahorse learns an extra Technical skill at levels
-- 2, 5, 7, 10 and 13; the text layer prints the 7 as a 1. Cache p038, flagged
-- for a corrupt glyph, matches its render on every number.
--
-- CONVENTIONS, stated so nobody re-derives them:
--   A creature's per-level M.D.C. or I.S.P. is in pools_note; the formula columns
--     hold what creature-roll.js can roll (PEx10, MEx2, 3D6x6+PE).
--   A cyborg NPC's mdc is the main body; its armor is in bonuses_note. A P.E.
--     printed n/a is left out of attributes. A Spd printed only in mph is left
--     out and stated in bonuses_note. Where the book prints a natural and a
--     bionic P.S. or P.P., attributes holds the natural figure.
--   An attack whose damage the book prints with no S.D.C. or M.D. unit is stored
--     with is_mega_damage 0 and says so in its note (Romanov's rune dagger and
--     body throw, Sokolov's kick).
--
-- AS PRINTED, and probably the book's own errors:
--   Kolodenko's Hit Points 73 / S.D.C. 42 and his Personal Resources line are
--     word for word Burgasov's.
--   Orloff and Romanov each print two skills twice at different percentages; the
--     first figure is stored and the second is in skills_note.
--   Nikoforov's Quick Stats print no M.D.C. number, no skills and no bonuses.
--
-- The Mega-Steeds are animals and playable 0. The True Megahorse is intelligent
-- and the book allows one as a player character in theory; that is in occ_note.




-- Read the result back. This script asserts its OWN rows and nothing else.
SELECT 'all 5 creatures are in' AS assertion, count(*) AS got, 5 AS want
  FROM creatures WHERE slug IN ('true-megahorse', 'horned-steed', 'burkov-mastodon', 'steppe-ostrich', 'ursan-forest-steed');
SELECT 'and 0 of them are playable' AS assertion, count(*) AS got, 0 AS want
  FROM creatures WHERE playable = 1 AND slug IN ('true-megahorse', 'horned-steed', 'burkov-mastodon', 'steppe-ostrich', 'ursan-forest-steed');
SELECT 'all 8 notable NPCs are in' AS assertion, count(*) AS got, 8 AS want
  FROM notable_npcs WHERE slug IN ('warlord-yuri-alekseyevna', 'warlord-pyotr-burgasov', 'warlord-stephan-kolodenko', 'warlord-boris-orloff', 'warlord-sonya-romanov', 'warlord-igor-seriyev', 'warlord-grigori-sokolov', 'general-katya-nikoforov');
SELECT 'the creatures carry 40 attacks' AS assertion, count(*) AS got, 40 AS want
  FROM stat_attacks WHERE owner_kind = 'creature' AND owner_slug IN ('true-megahorse', 'horned-steed', 'burkov-mastodon', 'steppe-ostrich', 'ursan-forest-steed');
SELECT 'and the notables 4' AS assertion, count(*) AS got, 4 AS want
  FROM stat_attacks WHERE owner_kind = 'notable_npc' AND owner_slug IN ('warlord-yuri-alekseyevna', 'warlord-pyotr-burgasov', 'warlord-stephan-kolodenko', 'warlord-boris-orloff', 'warlord-sonya-romanov', 'warlord-igor-seriyev', 'warlord-grigori-sokolov', 'general-katya-nikoforov');

-- Records this run. See db/migrations/024-data-script-runs.sql.
